The tables are created and filled as follows.

```sql
CREATE TABLE Student (sid TEXT PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE Course  (cid TEXT PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE Enroll (
  sid TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES Student(sid),
  cid TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES Course(cid),
  PRIMARY KEY (sid, cid)
);
INSERT INTO Student VALUES ('s1'), ('s2'), ('s3');
INSERT INTO Course  VALUES ('c1'), ('c2');
INSERT INTO Enroll  VALUES ('s1','c1'), ('s2','c1'), ('s3','c2');
```

Each insertion below is tried separately on these tables. Which are **rejected**?

The tables are created as follows (the DBMS enforces all constraints).

```sql
CREATE TABLE Dept (did TEXT PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE Emp (
  eid TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  did TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES Dept(did) ON DELETE SET NULL
);
```

Dept holds d1, d2. Emp holds (e1, d1), (e2, d2), (e3, d1). What happens on `DELETE FROM Dept WHERE did = 'd1';`?
